# The principals' web app (PRD E12-S5). Copy to .env.local only if you need to change something. Never commit real secrets.
# Nothing is required: the app talks to the firm's Supabase project, whose URL and public (publishable) key are committed in
# web/lib/env.mjs. Row-level security does the protecting; the publishable key alone can read nothing.
# To point a local copy at another project (a test one), set both of these:
# WEB_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-test-project-ref.supabase.co
# WEB_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-test-key
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and the NEXT_PUBLIC_ copies are no longer read by the web app.
# Optional: where the engine (the repository root, with src/ and the rule files) is at runtime. Defaults to the folder above web/.
# ENGINE_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/repo
# NEVER put a service-role or sb_secret_ key here. The web app acts only as the signed-in principal.
